From e93134c9c96a7805dbcfafd1508828ca691e8629 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrey Borodin <amborodin@acm.org>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 17:31:25 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] nbtree: WAL-log page merges

AB: bne cautionus, it all is generated without any human attention

A page merge changes the left page, right page, and parent as one
logical operation.  A critical section alone cannot make those changes
atomic on disk, and a standby cannot reproduce them without WAL.

Introduce a btree merge record that forces a full-page image for every
affected buffer.  This deliberately simple initial format makes redo
independent of the pre-record contents of all three pages.  Also WAL-log
each restartable merge-group cleanup transition, set page LSNs, and add
rmgr identification and description support.
